Okay, since I haven't seen anyone else contributing feedback on the
Convict quest, I went ahead and used wizard mode to artificially
enhance my success at playing the role and, thus, have been able
to have a look at the quest, so I can contribute some first-run
feedback.  I won't be able to comment much on difficulty, since
wizard mode tends to obscure some of those issues, but at least
I can pass a second set of eyeballs over the thing...

I'm using version 0.4 of the patch.  (I'd already started this
game before 0.5 was released.)

First thing I noticed was that when I ran into the quest portal
I got an interesting error message:

   create_monster: can't find feature "(null)"  Program in
   disorder - you should probably S)ave and reload the game.

The story (so far) is okay.  It could probably be polished in
a few places, but it's good enough for government work.

One thing that doesn't appear to be explained in the text, and
should be, is the presence of the altar on the quest home level.
I believe I understand the reason for having it there, from a
gameplay perspective, but the text that you get when you first
step onto the level should at least say something about Robert
having taken up a position in the prison chapel, or something.

It's not clear what the difference is, if any, between an "inmate"
(black @) and a "peaceful prisoner" (white @), other than which
level they're on and possibly whether their cell door is open or
not.  I'm not sure this matters, but if you did have something
particular in mind it's not really getting across, at least to me.

The first two levels (quest home and upper filler) seemed
rather...  empty.  The text mentions corrupt guards, but
there don't appear to be any.  (Maybe that explains the
"can't find feature" error?)  The filler level, particularly,
was *completely* uneventful -- just me and my pets, unless
you count the peaceful prisoners, whom I couldn't even
interact with because they were behind bars.

The third level (quest locate) is somewhat more interesting.
That's where I am so far, and I have to go get ready for
work now, so...  more comments later.


